WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.550
Since 1970, the world has lost about
411 million hectares of wetlands:

2
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.910
roughly 22 per cent.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:13.350
And losses continue, at
0.52 per cent a year.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.950
Florida's Everglades
were a River of Grass,

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.690
flowing slowly from the
Kissimmee River to Florida Bay.

6
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.150
Then canals and levees drained
land for farms and homes.

7
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.990
Can a plan for a whole
basin bring a wetland back?

8
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.690
Quickly and cheaply?

9
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.930
Or never?

10
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.430
In this mission, you'll learn
integrated drainage basin management,

11
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.870
and test it on Australia's
Murray-Darling Basin.

12
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.250
Then you'll judge which scale of
water management makes the difference,

13
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.970
and for whom.

14
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.530
Your mission: decide whether a plan for
a whole river basin can bring a wetland

15
00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:47.230
back.
